# What the CLOUDFLARE deployment does NOT serve.
#
# Scope, because it is easy to over-read this file: it applies to the
# Cloudflare Worker in `wrangler.jsonc` — the `mobius-nav` deployment — and
# to nothing else. It has no effect on GitHub Pages, which serves the three
# BACS prototypes and publishes the repository verbatim.
#
# It is also not a privacy control. **This repository is public**, so the
# specs and the Figma frames are readable on github.com and on GitHub Pages
# whatever this file says. What it does is keep the Cloudflare deployment to
# what it is for: `wrangler.jsonc` points at the repository root, so without
# this file that Worker publishes the whole tree, which is simply more
# surface than it needs.
#
# Same pattern format as .gitignore, but written as a plain blocklist with no
# negation: gitignore cannot re-include a file underneath an excluded
# directory, and quietly publishing something because a clever pattern did
# not do what it looked like it did is not a risk worth taking.
#
# What stays public, and all that needs to be:
#
#     prototypes/**/*.html .css .js     the prototypes themselves
#     css/buckholt.css                  the runtime they load
#     css/buckholt-ai-fixes.css
#     components/*/*.js                 dropdown.js and form.js are loaded by
#                                       the pages; tabs.js is the same kind of
#                                       thing and is design-system runtime
#
# Checked: nothing a running prototype loads is excluded below — the pages
# reach outside their own folder for exactly those four files, and no HTML,
# CSS or JS anywhere references a .png.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- tooling
.git/**
.github/**
.wrangler/**
node_modules/**
wrangler.json
wrangler.jsonc
wrangler.toml
.assetsignore
.gitignore
.cursorrules

# -------------------------------------------------------- unreleased design
# The Figma frames behind every prototype: unreleased product design, and the
# bulk of the repository. Only the specs link to them, and the specs are not
# served either.
**/screenshots/**
**/*.png
**/*.jpg
**/*.jpeg
**/*.gif
**/*.svg

# ------------------------------------------------------- specs and internals
# Every spec, every PROTOTYPE.md and SPEC-CHANGES.md, every README, the agent
# rules, the discrepancy and verification records. None of it is needed to
# run a prototype and all of it is internal.
**/*.md

# Reference material taken from the live product.
prototypes/Mobius-navigation/reference/**
**/*.xlsx
**/*.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------- Buckholt's own documents
# 40 saved pages from buck.88mph.design. They are the markup evidence the
# parity check reads; they are not ours to republish.
code-specs-html/**

# ------------------------------------------------------- docs and test pages
# `components/*/examples.html` and the pattern pages are documentation; the
# style guide and the runtime harness in `tools/` are for the team, not the
# public. The component *scripts* stay: the prototypes load them.
components/**/*.html
patterns/**
foundations/**
responsive/**
discrepancies/**
verification/**
test/**
tools/**
